# One row for each type: its kind (nut, stud or standoff), the diameter
# of its mounting hole, the least sheet thickness, the least distance
# from the center of the hole to an edge or a bend line, its thread, and
# the diameter and the height of its body, a plain cylinder that stands
# on the sheet over the hole (for a stud, its post), with the material
# of the library that the body takes, in the units of plicad(7).  A
# flush type fills its hole too, and may have no body over the sheet
# (BODY_H 0); a blind one sits in a hole DEPTH deep from the face it
# stands on (insert.h).  The metric rows are usual sizes of such
# hardware; the data of the maker of a part has the last word.
